Okok Recipe

Ingredients:

1kg fresh okok leaves

500g groundnuts

250ml red palm oil

500g beef or cow skin

200g smoked fish

1 cup ground crayfish

2 seasoning cubes

Salt to taste

Fresh pepper to taste

Water as needed

Preparation:

Wash the okok leaves thoroughly and cut them into small pieces if necessary.

Roast the groundnuts lightly, remove the skins, and grind them into a smooth paste.

Wash the beef and cow skin. Put them in a pot with salt, seasoning cubes, and a little water. Cook until tender.

Add the smoked fish and ground crayfish to the meat and stir well.

Add the okok leaves and mix thoroughly. Cook for about 10–15 minutes until the leaves soften.

Add the groundnut paste, palm oil, and pepper. Stir well to combine all the ingredients.

Add a little water if necessary and simmer over low heat for 20–30 minutes, stirring occasionally to prevent sticking.

Taste and adjust the salt and seasoning. Cook until the groundnut mixture is well combined with the leaves and the sauce is rich and thick.

Serve hot with water fufu, garri, or boiled plantains.
